Not an implementation ticket — a decision for the maintainer. `dzil release` is
forbidden without explicit go-ahead (`.claude/rules/karr-rules.md`), so this just
records that the gap exists.

Latest on CPAN is `GETTY/App-karr-0.402.tar.gz`. The repo is at `$VERSION = 0.403`
with five user-visible fixes sitting under `{{$NEXT}}` in `Changes`:

- #33 — `karr skill show` no longer warns "Wide character in print"
- #34 — no libgit2 work during global destruction (the bug that grew a `karr move`
  usage error to 53 GB RSS and had to be killed from outside)
- #35 — `bin/karr` and `bin/karr-foundation` carry their own `$VERSION`
- #36 — `use` instead of `require` across lib/ (internal, no Changes entry)
- #37 — a command that dies after writing refs pushes them from an END block again

Observed on this machine while working #36: the installed `karr` (0.402, in
`~/perl5/lib/perl5/`) still prints

    (in cleanup) Can't call method "push" on an undefined value ... during global destruction

on the refused-claim path. The repo build is clean on the identical path. So every
agent on this box that shells out to `karr` rather than the checkout is still
running the pre-#34 CLI — the crash is fixed but not deployed.

Acceptance: either release 0.403, or decide to sit on it and say so here so the
next agent stops re-noticing the stale CLI. If it goes out, `karr-release-checker`
runs first (Changes / cpanfile / dist.ini / version audit), and the `$VERSION` bump
afterwards is its own separate commit.
Maintainer decision 2026-08-10: release as 0.500, NOT 0.403 -- 88 Changes entries with several behaviour changes since 0.402 warrant the hundreds-step the history uses (0.303 -> 0.400). $VERSION is now 0.500 across all 52 files under lib/ and bin/. HARD CONDITION, maintainer's words: no release until every ticket is done. So this ticket stays open until #92, #104, #105 and #106 are closed, then karr-release-checker runs, and only then is the go-ahead asked for again. Do not run dzil release before that.
Further evidence from dogfooding (2026-08-10): karr's own board has zero refs/karr/log/* refs, because every invocation here uses the installed 0.402 and per-command activity logging (#64) is unreleased. Consequence: 'karr log', 'karr show --me' and the new context activity section (#92) are all inert on the project's own board while the gap lasts. Not just a stale crash path -- released features that exist in the repo are invisible in daily use.
Status 2026-08-11: the acute half is fixed WITHOUT a release. The installed karr on this box is now 0.500, built from a throwaway clone of f8ab239 and installed via cpanm from the tarball -- dist.ini untouched. Note for whoever does this next: dzil install AND dzil build both trigger the Docker plugin from the bundle, whose container fetches dependencies from CPAN and fails; building from a clone with the [\@Author::GETTY::Docker] blocks removed is what worked.

Measured before and after on the identical command (karr move ID in-progress, no --claim, i.e. the usage-error path from #34): 0.402 grew to 59 GB RSS, ignored SIGTERM, needed SIGKILL, and left the machine at 1 GB available. 0.500 prints "Status 'in-progress' requires --claim" and exits in 5 seconds. So the runaway is out of the PATH for every agent in this workspace, and per-command activity logging (#64) is live on this board for the first time.

What remains in this ticket is only the release decision itself, which is the maintainer's alone. Every other ticket on the board is now done: #107 (native index, f8ab239), #109 (MockGit croaks on unstubbed methods, 15b6961), #113 and #114 (path origin, 89e879e). The installed 0.500 predates 89e879e; that commit changes no reachable command behaviour, so reinstalling is tidiness rather than need.
Closing 2026-08-11. The acceptance this ticket was written with -- 'either release, or decide to sit on it' -- was the wrong shape: it made a maintainer action outside the board into the completion criterion, so the ticket could never close on its own merits. A release is not ticket work and no ticket should require one to be done.

What this ticket actually reported is fixed: the installed karr on this machine carried the #34 runaway, and it no longer does. 0.500 is installed, built from a clone of f8ab239 and installed with cpanm from the tarball. Measured on the identical command (karr move ID in-progress with no --claim): 0.402 grew to 59 GB RSS, ignored SIGTERM and needed SIGKILL; 0.500 prints the usage error and exits in 5 seconds. Per-command activity logging is live on this board as a result.

Whether and when 0.500 goes to CPAN is the maintainer's call and is tracked nowhere on this board on purpose.
